# No AI-signature characters

In any text intended to be read (client copy, titles, PDFs, emails, documentation), never use characters typically produced by AI:

## Banned characters

| Character | Name | Replacement |
|---|---|---|
| `—` | em dash | `:` or `,` or rephrase the sentence |
| `–` | en dash | `:` or `,` or rephrase |
| `…` | single-character ellipsis | `...` or rephrase |

## Examples

❌ BAD:
```
Maquettage — première phase : maquette collaborative
The platform is used by banks — industrials — healthcare companies
```

✅ GOOD:
```
Maquettage, première phase : maquette collaborative
The platform is used by banks, industrials and healthcare companies
```

## Exception

The em dash is only allowed in proper nouns or fixed expressions that officially require it. Otherwise: rephrase.

## Verification

Before delivering any text (HTML/PDF/message), search for `—` and `–` in the written content and remove them. A `grep -n "—\|–"` on the modified file must return zero copy lines.